# === Oshiire: secrets & personal data — MUST stay out of git ===

# Reddit API credentials and any other secrets.
# These never get committed. Losing this line = burned secret.
.env
.env.*
*.secret
praw.ini
!.env.example

# Personal data derived from YOUR Reddit account.
# The manifest holds your saved-post titles/URLs; the folders hold your images.
# None of this belongs in a remote, even a private one.
staging/
# Guard for the default-config case only. The archive normally lives OUTSIDE the
# repo -- ARCHIVE_DIR in .env is an absolute path, and nothing in the project
# writes to a relative `archive/`. This rule matches nothing in a correctly
# configured checkout; it is here so that someone who points ARCHIVE_DIR at
# `./archive` while trying things out cannot commit their images by accident.
archive/
manifest.json
*.manifest.json
!manifest.example.json

# Personal archive layout (describes YOUR whole collection). Templates are
# committed; the real ones are yours and stay local.
layout.json
layout copy.json
000___Known_Series_Names.txt
known_series_names.txt
!layout.example.json
!known_series_names.example.txt

# Alternate series names you've taught resolve.py (variant -> canonical).
# Same class as subreddit_map.json: reveals your specific collection in detail.
# Template is committed; the real one is yours and stays local.
data/series_aliases.json
!data/series_aliases.example.json

# Personal subreddit->franchise map -- reveals your specific fandom/taste in
# detail. Template is committed; the real one is yours and stays local.
subreddit_map.json
!subreddit_map.example.json

# Perceptual-hash index of the local archive (hash_index.py). Derived cache of
# your personal archive contents -- stays local.
data/archive_index.db
data/archive_index.db-journal
data/archive_index.db-wal
data/archive_index.db-shm

# Reddit saved-posts export -- personal account data. Template is committed so
# the backfill sweep can be dry-run before you request your own export.
data/saved_posts.csv
!data/saved_posts.example.csv

# Bulk-unsave whitelist built by export_unsave_list.py from the manifest +
# backfill log -- a list of YOUR post ids. Account-derived; stays local.
data/unsave_list.json
!data/unsave_list.example.json

# Perceptual-hash signatures of image-host "removed" placeholder cards
# (tombstones.py). Deliberately NOT ignored: host placeholders are the same for
# everyone, so this is generic reference data, not account-derived. Listed here
# only so its absence from the ignore rules reads as a decision, not an
# oversight.
#   data/tombstones.json  <- committed on purpose

# AI model weights — large binaries, don't want them in git regardless.
*.onnx
*.pt
*.pth
models/

# === Standard Python ===
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
# Virtualenvs. `.venv*/` and not `.venv/`: this project keeps more than one --
# `.venv-win` (Windows, py3.14) alongside `.venv` (Linux, py3.12) -- and a
# literal `.venv/` matches neither the suffixed name nor any future variant.
# .venv-win alone is ~20,000 files / ~680 MB of site-packages (numpy, scipy,
# opencv-contrib, onnxruntime, gradio, pandas, scikit-learn, plus .libs binary
# trees), so a miss here is not a small mistake. Verify by EXIT CODE, not by
# `-v` output -- a negation match also exits 0, which reads as a false
# "ignored":
#     git check-ignore -q .venv-win/ && echo ignored
.venv*/
venv/
env/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/


# === OS / editor cruft ===
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/

# Claude Code local state. Currently holds only settings.local.json (per-machine
# tool-permission grants) and scheduled_tasks.lock (a session id + pid), neither
# of which is shareable or meaningful on another machine. The whole directory is
# ignored rather than just those two files: if project-level slash commands or
# agents are added later they'd live under .claude/commands/ or .claude/agents/,
# and those WOULD be worth publishing -- at which point narrow this to
# `.claude/settings.local.json` + `.claude/*.lock` instead of widening what
# leaks by default.
.claude/

calibration/

# Back-catalogue backfill working dir (backfill.py): resumable cursor, run log,
# and temp downloads -- all derived from your personal CSV + archive. Stays local.
#
# Written as `data/backfill/*` and NOT `data/backfill/`: git cannot re-include a
# file underneath an EXCLUDED DIRECTORY, so with a trailing-slash rule here the
# `!` line below would silently do nothing (git never descends into the dir to
# see it). Excluding the dir's *contents* instead leaves the directory itself
# traversable, so the committed .example.* templates survive. Verify with:
#     git check-ignore -v data/backfill/state.json          # -> ignored
#     git check-ignore -v data/backfill/state.example.json  # -> no match
data/backfill/*
!data/backfill/*.example.*

# Internal working notes: open work, settled decisions, release TODOs. Not part
# of the public release -- CLAUDE.md and docs/SETUP.md are what ship.
docs/PROJECT_CONTEXT.md

# Scratch scripts stay local, but one-off data MIGRATIONS are committed: they
# rename and move files inside ARCHIVE_DIR, which is not itself in version
# control, so the script is the only record of what was changed and the only
# way to reason about it afterwards. `scripts/*` rather than `scripts/` because
# git will not descend into an excluded directory -- the negation below can
# only re-include migrations/ if the parent itself is not excluded.
scripts/*
!scripts/migrations/
authtest.py
cookietest.py
